  <knowledge>
    - Programs may optionally use System.err for error messages.
    - When printing the winning path, use the same board representation except relevant hexagons are
   shown as `*` (path or connected to path).
    - At the start of the first game print a greeting `Welcome to Prime` (or `Welcome to [game
  name]` for new-game) and indicate which player is to move first.
    - Empty hexagons are displayed as a dot `.` when printing the board.
    - Red-occupied hexagons are displayed as `X` and blue-occupied hexagons as `O` in `print`
  output.
    - Within a row, each hexagon is separated from the next by a single space character.
    - A successful `place` produces no confirmation; instead print `[player name]'s turn` for the
  next player when there is a next turn.
    - On victory print `[player name] wins!` and output the winning path.
  </knowledge>
